Printing Tips:
All parts are oriented correctly for printing
0.4 mm nozzle;
Layer thickness: 0.2 mm;
Set the supports to a 75-degree angle. This ensures supports are only placed where needed.
Infill: 20–100%;
Smoothing (optional).
Number of walls – 4
Number of top and bottom layers – 4
Also, make sure the part is securely attached to the build plate. I use a thin layer of PVA glue. Or I simply wipe the surface thoroughly with alcohol. It’s important that the edges of the base and lid don’t peel away during printing; this will ensure the box looks the way you intended. You can add a “brim” when printing the main parts—this will provide better adhesion, especially at the corners.
